<title>JAPAN: NTT aims to recover Sri Lanka investment in 10 yrs.</title>
<headline>NTT aims to recover Sri Lanka investment in 10 yrs.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nippon Telegraph and Telephone Corp (NTT) said on Tuesday that it aims to recover its $225 million investment in Sri Lanka Telecom in about 10 years.  </p>
<p>&quot;We expect the telephone business in Sri Lanka will yield profits and we hope to recover our investment in about 10 years in management fees and other investment returns,&quot; Mitsuhiro Takase, NTT's manager in charge of international operations, told a news conference.</p>
<p>Takase also said Sri Lanka will become an important base for NTT as it tries to build a telecommunications network in Asia.</p>
</text>
